# Extensionless, so the Prettier CLI infers no parser and skips it, but VS Code
# detects it as Markdown and the editor extension formats it on save. That
# rewrites the catch-all `*` rule into a Markdown bullet `-`, which silently
# turns "everyone owns everything" into "someone owns a file named -", with
# format:check still green. The extension honours this file, so this entry is
# what actually stops it.
.github/CODEOWNERS
